From: lights-out-fixtures <fixtures@lights-out.invalid>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 06:23:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Refuse a meetup capacity below one with 422
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

POST /api/meetups validated capacity only as an integer, so 0 or a
negative number created a meetup that answered 409 "meetup is full" to
its first registration. MeetupCreateRequest now requires capacity >= 1;
FastAPI answers 422 before anything is created. The README row for the
route says so.

Hand-written L0 fixture for ticket 0012's impl member (docs/adr/0036 §7):
no model wrote this change.
---
 app/README.md              | 2 +-
 app/backend/meetups/app.py | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/README.md b/app/README.md
index 6dbef50..f55fcae 100644
--- a/app/README.md
+++ b/app/README.md
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ FastAPI backend + Postgres + React frontend. Demonstrates the core platform feat
 | `POST /api/signup` | no | `{email,password}` → 201; 409 if email exists |
 | `POST /api/login` | no | → `{token}`; 401 on bad credentials |
 | `GET /api/meetups`, `GET /api/meetups/{id}` | no | list / one, with `venue_lat`/`venue_lon` |
-| `POST /api/meetups` | bearer | `{title,starts_at,venue,capacity}` → 201; geocodes `venue` |
+| `POST /api/meetups` | bearer | `{title,starts_at,venue,capacity}` → 201; geocodes `venue`; `capacity` below 1 → 422 |
 | `POST /api/meetups/{id}/registrations` | bearer | 201; 409 when full and flag `waitlist` off; 501 when full and flag on |
 | `GET /healthz` | no | `{"status":"ok","version":APP_VERSION}` after `SELECT 1`; 503 otherwise |
 | `GET /metrics` | no | Prometheus text |
diff --git a/app/backend/meetups/app.py b/app/backend/meetups/app.py
index 0dd05bc..7e3a482 100644
--- a/app/backend/meetups/app.py
+++ b/app/backend/meetups/app.py
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ import psycopg
 from fastapi import Depends, FastAPI, HTTPException, Response
 from fastapi.staticfiles import StaticFiles
 from psycopg import errors as pg_errors
-from pydantic import BaseModel
+from pydantic import BaseModel, Field
 
 from meetups.auth import current_user_id, hash_password, issue_session, verify_password
 from meetups.db import get_db
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ class MeetupCreateRequest(BaseModel):
     title: str
     starts_at: str
     venue: str
-    capacity: int
+    capacity: int = Field(ge=1)
 
 
 def _meetup_row(row: tuple) -> dict:
